	(text "NOTES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 328.93 144.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.048 3.048)
				(thickness 0.381)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8bbb2568-c5d8-4505-afd1-b7fe712f5cf3")
	)
	(text "Set R_CAL until this node is exactly 3.3V\nat the working temperature (38C)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 75.946 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9cc90ff6-087c-44a6-8636-5c2d1b5ca970")
	)
	(text "TEMP COMPENSATION: SSI2164s have temp drift of <= +0.13dB/C, due to I_C = I_S(e^(qV_BE / kT) - 1).\nThe LM334 is used to stretch the CV with temp changes to cancel this out. It sources 227 microvolts\nper deg C/K through the 226 ohm resistor which is a standard resistor, this effect is also b/c of \nBJTs and kT/q effect, so has the same exponential/log scale.\n\nV_R = 227uV/K * T, from LM334 physics, T temperature Kelvin\nIset = V_R / R_set. Internal bias term adds 6%, Itotal = 1.06Iset (all from datasheet)\nV_ref = Itotal*R_L\n=> V_ref = 1.06(227uV/K * T * R_L) / R_set.\n\nSet T to 38C = 310K, a bit warmer than ambient that we expect the silicon to run around.\nThis is our \"nominal\" case, where we want V_ref to be exactly 3.30V for the DAC reference (no scaling)\n=> R_set = 1.06 * 227uV/K * 310K / Itotal, R_L = V_ref / Itotal\nPick an Itotal well under 1mA, to keep self-heating low. Pick Itotal = 330uA => R_L = 10k = common value\nAND R_set = 1.06 * 227u * 310 / 330u = 226 ohms.\nSO V_ref = 1.06(227uV/K * T * R_L) / R_set. => V_ref = 0.010647V * T and @ 330K, V_ref = 3.3V\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 290.068 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c1b607db-07d0-4cb8-8722-a3ec9fcf301e")
	)
	(text "PIN 1 (MODE) is left N/C (no R_M), causing the VCAs to operate as class A/B amplifiers rather \nthan class A. This is because:\n\nClass A will make the chip hotter and make it drift more\n\nClass A is noisier and the signal is meant to be summed with many others as an auxliary send\nbus, so noise will add up.\n\nThe higher THD with class A/B is fine for just sends and does not scale like noise does."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.798 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "cceed90d-738c-4307-ac5d-eef816982439")
	)
	(text "These buffer the control voltage into the SSI2164 inputs.\nThey also apply a low pass filter (fc = 234Hz, -3dB) and\nmap the 0-3.3V range from the DACs to -0.2-3.3V, giving a\ngain range of +6dB to -100dB for the VCAs\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.172 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "dc0435c5-2f02-4eac-8ba3-6bd843bf7983")
	)
	(text "CV buffer:\nCV from DAC between 0 and 3.3V is non inverting: V1 = V_C * [1 + (R_F/R_G)]\nReference voltage is inverting. it scales up as temp goes up, so the buffered\nCV goes up as temp goes up "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 296.926 225.806 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e29d6446-386e-4486-a039-35e018995f39")
	)
